  "interpretation": [
    "Frontier support utilization is real: 62.85% of recovery switches select a non-historical-RVR representative, so V36 did not degenerate to the old binary endpoint.",
    "But broader existing-bank support is not sufficient: collision returns to 34/48, identical to COWP and 7 worse than V35 CPOSH; relative to V35, V36 has 1 rescue and 8 induced collisions (McNemar p=0.0391).",
    "Weak-dominance continuation is much more permissive than strict entry (mean weak admissible 6.42 vs strict 0.58 reps); recovery active/continue rates expand to 34.4%/31.1%.",
    "In V36-induced scenes recovery is active ~80.4% and continues ~76.7%, while zero-conventional exposure is ~92.5% and mean conventional candidates only ~0.79. All six induced collisions are immediately preceded by an uncertified recovery candidate with collision_safe=false and prefix=0.",
    "Non-RVR selection and prefix gain do not distinguish rescue from harm: non-RVR switch rate is ~77.4% in rescued vs ~75.0% in induced, selected prefix delta ~5.20 vs ~5.36. Therefore semantic option richness/current prefix are not returnability.",
    "The dominant missing object is an explicit control-reachable return path to the conventional-feasible set, not another spectrum/frontier scalar or broader semantic selector."
  ]
